    <!-- Step sync setup guide -->
    <string name="settings_step_sync_setup_hint">Make sure the target app is linked to Health Connect with step-reading and background access.</string>
    <string name="settings_step_sync_setup_open">View setup guide</string>
    <string name="step_setup_title">Step sync setup guide</string>
    <string name="step_setup_intro">This app writes simulated steps to Health Connect, and the target app reads them directly from Health Connect. Activity trackers such as Google Health can also connect to Health Connect to provide everyday phone or wearable steps.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_chain">This app → Health Connect → target app</string>
    <string name="step_setup_1_title">1. Get Health Connect ready</string>
    <string name="step_setup_1_body">Built into Android 14 and later — nothing to install. Older versions need Health Connect from the Play Store.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_2_title">2. Allow this app to write steps</string>
    <string name="step_setup_2_body">This grant lets the app convert simulated travel distance into steps and write them to Health Connect. Write access only — it never reads any of your health data.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_3_title">3. Let the target app read Health Connect</string>
    <string name="step_setup_3_body">Choose Health Connect as the step source in the target app. Then open Health Connect → App permissions → the target app and allow it to read Steps. If Add access is available, also allow background data access.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_pikmin_note">Pikmin Bloom example (Android 14+ only): Settings → Privacy &amp; Steps → Steps → Health Connect → Open settings. In Health Connect, choose Allow all for Pikmin Bloom, then use Add access to allow background data access. On Android 13 or earlier, phone tracking is the only option and cannot read simulated steps written by this app.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_4_title">4. Link Google Health with Health Connect</string>
    <string name="step_setup_4_body">From Health Connect: open App permissions → (Google) Health → Permissions → Fitness &amp; wellness, then allow Steps under Read permissions.\n\nFrom Google Health: tap Health at the bottom right → Focus → Sync all health apps → Set up → Set up again → agree to sync with Health Connect → select Fitness &amp; wellness data → Continue. Allow Steps, past fitness and wellness data, and background fitness and wellness data, then tap Done.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_5_title">5. Verify the result</string>
    <string name="step_setup_5_body">Start a simulation and first confirm that Written today keeps increasing in this app, then open the target app and check its step count. Health Connect sync can take a few minutes. If it is still unchanged, restart the target app and check its step-reading and background permissions again.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_troubleshoot">If steps do not appear, check in order:\n\n1. This app → Health Connect: data is written in batches every 10–25 seconds; use Written today to confirm.\n\n2. Health Connect → target app: confirm the target app can read Steps in the background and has Health Connect selected as its step source.\n\n3. Everyday activity source: if the target app requires an activity tracker, confirm Google Health has Steps, history, and background access.\n\nSync is not instant. Wait a few minutes, restart the target app, and turn off battery saver if it restricts background sync.</string>
    <string name="step_setup_action_open_hc_settings">Open Health Connect settings</string>
    <!-- Too-fast-for-steps notice -->
    <string name="step_too_fast_title">Too fast — steps not counted</string>
    <string name="step_too_fast_body">The simulated speed is above 20 km/h, beyond any plausible walking or running pace, so this stretch is not converted into steps. Drop below 20 km/h to resume counting.</string>
    <string name="route_speed_exceeds_step_limit">Above %1$d km/h — this movement will not count as steps</string>
    <string name="step_setup_speed_limit_note">About simulated speed: only movement at or below %1$d km/h is converted into steps; anything faster is skipped because it is beyond any plausible walking or running pace. The Walk and Bike presets stay within range; Drive produces no steps. Jump-mode teleports are never counted either.</string>
